# Angular → Flutter Migration: Silverwind Frontend

## Analysis Summary

### Angular Architecture Overview

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Framework** | Angular 21 (standalone components, signals-based state) |
| **Styling** | TailwindCSS 4 + Angular Material 21 + Custom CSS variables |
| **HTTP** | Angular HttpClient with 5 interceptors |
| **State** | Signal-based [AuthStore](file:///Users/manishmachha/Desktop/MyWorkspace/solventek-silverwind/silverwind-frontend/src/app/core/stores/auth.store.ts#22-180) with `sessionStorage` persistence |
| **Routing** | Angular Router with lazy-loaded routes, 2 guards (auth + role) |
| **Auth** | JWT Bearer tokens, role-based access (6 roles, 2 org types) |
| **Charts** | Chart.js via ng2-charts |
| **Markdown** | ngx-markdown |
| **Icons** | Bootstrap Icons |

### Feature Modules (17 total)

| Module | Components | Routes |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| Dashboard | Role-based dashboard | `/dashboard` |
| Admin | Employee list/detail, Audit logs | `/admin/employees`, `/admin/employees/:id`, `/admin/audit-logs` |
| Vendors | List, Detail | `/vendors`, `/vendors/:id` |
| Jobs | List, Create/Edit, Detail | `/jobs`, `/jobs/create`, `/jobs/edit/:id`, `/jobs/:id` |
| Applications | List, Detail, Vendor list, Track list | `/applications`, `/applications/:id`, `/vendor-applications`, `/track-applications` |
| Candidates | List, Form, Detail | `/candidates`, `/candidates/new`, `/candidates/edit/:id`, `/candidates/:id` |
| Projects | List, Detail | `/projects`, `/projects/:id` |
| Clients | List, Detail | `/clients`, `/clients/:id` |
| Tickets | List, Detail | `/portal/tickets`, `/portal/tickets/:id` |
| Holidays | List | `/holidays` |
| Assets | Management, My Assets | `/admin/assets`, `/my-assets` |
| Payroll | Management, My Payslips | `/admin/payroll`, `/my-payslips` |
| Attendance | Management, My Attendance | `/admin/attendance`, `/my-attendance` |
| Leave | My Leaves, Management, Configuration | `/my-leaves`, `/admin/leave-management`, `/admin/leave-configuration` |
| Organization | Discovery, My Organization | `/organization/discovery`, `/organization/my-organization` |
| Notifications | List | `/notifications` |
| Profile | User Details | `/profile` |

### Public Pages (10+)

Home, About, Services, Careers, Case Studies, Leadership, Contact, Login, Tracking (Login + Dashboard), VMS

### Design System Extraction

```
Colors:
  Primary: #6366f1 (Indigo 500), Dark: #4f46e5, Light: #818cf8
  Secondary: #8b5cf6 (Violet 500), Dark: #7c3aed, Light: #a78bfa
  Surface: #f8fafc → #f1f5f9 → #e2e8f0 → #cbd5e1
  Text: Main #0f172a, Muted #64748b, Light #94a3b8
  Success: #10b981, Warning: #f59e0b, Danger: #ef4444, Info: #3b82f6

Typography: Inter font, system fallbacks
Gradients: Primary (135deg, indigo→violet), Success, Dark, Surface
Shadows: sm, md, lg, card, card-hover, glow
Border Radius: 0.75rem (inputs), 1rem (cards), 9999px (badges/avatars)
Transitions: fast (150ms), normal (300ms), cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)
```

### Auth Flow
1. User enters email/password → `POST /api/auth/login`
2. Backend returns `{ success, message, data: { accessToken, refreshToken, user } }`
3. Tokens stored in `sessionStorage` (→ Flutter Secure Storage)
4. JWT attached via interceptor to all `/api` requests
5. 401 → redirect to login, 403 → dialog with "Access Denied"
6. Role-based route guards check `user.role.name` and `user.orgType`

### API Pattern
- Base URL: `/api` (proxied to `http://localhost:9090`)
- Response envelope: `{ success: boolean, message: string, data: T }`
- Pagination: Spring Boot style `{ content, totalElements, totalPages, size, number, last }`
- Success mutations show snackbar from `response.message`
- Error responses show structured error messages

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **State Management Choice**: Riverpod is proposed over Bloc since Angular's signal-based reactive state maps directly to Riverpod's provider pattern. This is simpler for this project since there is only 1 store (`AuthStore`).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Project Location**: The Flutter app will be created at `/Users/manishmachha/Desktop/MyWorkspace/solventek-silverwind/silverwind-flutter`. Confirm this is acceptable.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Scope Prioritization**: This is a massive project (~60+ screens, 17 feature modules). I recommend building it in clear phases and verifying each phase. The implementation plan below covers ALL components, but execution will proceed phase by phase.

---

